WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
Hank: It’s the beach!

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:02.510
John: A couple of nerds at the beach.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.670
Hank: We’re actually quite far away from
the ocean 'cause there, there’s sharks in

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.670
there.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.540
John: Henry’s very nervous about orcas.
He keeps being, like, “Is an orca going

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.410
to eat me?” and I’m like “Well not if
you’re eight inches in the water."

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.410
Hank: Good morning John.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.410
John: Good morning Hank.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.410
Hank: It’s Friday.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.410
John: Yeah, it is Friday.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:21.350
Hank: Uh huh, ahh… how are your hotdog legs.
The infernal day star is shining its radiation

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.650
down upon us; I can feel it giving me cancer.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.570
John: Light is the visible sign of the invisible
light. That’s T. S. Elliot.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.910
Hank: It’s lovely but it, it doesn’t mean
anything to me.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.970
John: When I ask Henry what light is he always
says in his cute little four year old voice

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.510
“It’s the visible sign of the invisible
light." find that very adorable. Question

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.550
Friday, the day that we answer real questions
from real Nerdfighters. We took our laptop

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.570
down to the beach because that’s how we
roll. Am I on the screen? I’m a little worried

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.570
that you’re cropping me…

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.570
Hank: You’re there!

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:45.570
John: I’m worried that you’re cropping
me out.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.570
Hank: Yeah, it’s a really wide lens.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.570
John: Alright.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.570
Hank: Melissa wants to know “When is the
Art Assignment going to premiere?”

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.240
John: The first episode of the Art Assignment
comes out late February. Subscribe, link in

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.240
the dooblydoo.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.740
Hank: She also wants to know “Who the eff
is Hank?”

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:54.740
John: Ohhhh!

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.770
Hank: You weren’t prepared for this?!

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:59.520
John: I waah, ahhh, ahh, I’m never ready!
Hank is the second largest ocean on Earth!

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.829
Hank: I don’t even know which one that is.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:01.829
John: That’s this one!

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:02.829
Hank: Oh.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:03.829
John No, I think this is the Gulf, but whatever.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:08.740
Hank: If you two were fighting and your only
weapons were the object to your left, how

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.869
would you use them and who would win?

00:01:10.869 --> 00:01:11.869
John: You have a chair.

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:14.501
Hank: Either that or you. I could just beat
you with you. Why are you hitting yourself?

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.060
John: I just have the sand.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.060
Hank: Nah ha! It's a computer!

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.829
John: I would sand Hank’s computer because
there is nothing that would upset him more.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:22.829
He would panic.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:25.569
Hank: Danny want to know “How come Dave
Green is never in the videos?”

00:01:25.569 --> 00:01:26.569
John: Who’s Dave?

00:01:26.569 --> 00:01:30.310
Hank: The third unsuccessful brother. Dave
has been made up by a Tumblr.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.869
John: How did this happen and I didn’t even
know about it? Suddenly I have an imaginary

00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:35.869
brother.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:39.130
Hank: Amy wants to know “Why is love so
hard?” (Singing) What is love?

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.529
Both: (Singing) Don’t hurt me, no more.

00:01:41.529 --> 00:01:43.409
Hank: That was really not even close.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:45.340
John: People on the beach are looking at us
funny by the way.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.909
Both: (Singing) The people on the beach they
think that we’re crazy. The people on the

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:50.509
beach they think that we’re crazy.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:53.079
John: It should always be a little bit of
work because it matters.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.439
Hank: Yeah, If you th… Yeah, that’s true.

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:56.419
John: Anyway, there’s all different kinds
of love.

00:01:56.419 --> 00:01:58.929
Hank: There’s all different kinds of farts.

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:03.179
John: (laughs) This is a really good YouTube
video. We should, we should do this, we should

00:02:03.179 --> 00:02:04.179
do this more often.

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:06.819
Hank: In comments tell me all the different
kinds of farts.

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:09.500
John: No, in comments tell us about Dave Green.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:14.110
Hank: Just… I need that. No I need that
John. We need that for the rest of video.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.110
John: I know.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:20.930
Hank: So… So go get some glue. Beautiful.
Wendy wants to know “Which of you has the

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.379
worst glasses prescription?”

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:26.340
John: I don’t know. Let’s take a switcheroo
here. Definitely me.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.620
Hank: Yeah, definitely you. Wow!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.620
John: Wait until you’re old.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.260
Hank: I am on acid right now. Well yours is
very sharp but none of the things are lining

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.260
up.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.379
John: You know, your left, your left eye is
almost identical to my left eye. Your right

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:38.379
eye is…

00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:39.379
Hank: Yeah the right eye.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:40.379
John: Super weird. Who looks better in the
others glass…?

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:41.840
Hank: Do I look like a naughty professor?

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.430
John: Who looks better in the others glasses?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.970
Hank: Is that, is that a thing? Naughty professor?

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:50.269
John: I don’t think so. I think you made
that up. It’s a… What is it? It’s nutty.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.510
A nutty professor. That’s what you were
thinking of.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.940
Hank: Oh, I wanted to ask, uh, if you could
tell me anything about The Fault in Our Stars

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.940
trailer.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:03.800
John: Ahh, umm, grrr, umm, mmm! It will come
out soon in the next few weeks and, um, yes.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.549
I have seen it. I thought it was truly excellent.
I hope other people like it too. I’m very

00:03:08.549 --> 00:03:10.599
nervous for everyone to see it but hopefully
soon.

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:13.849
Hank: John, thanks for being on a… question
video with me.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:14.849
John: Oh no thanks for…

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:18.310
Hank: And taking me here to Florida where
I probably got a sun burn just in the last

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.310
twenty minutes.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:20.310
John: I have sunscreen on.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.310
Hank: I didn’t do that.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.569
John: Best wishes. We need to wrap up this
video.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:28.330
Hank: I need to go because I’m… I may
actually not survive this. Uh, I’ll see

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.330
you on Tuesday.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.330
​(music)

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.330
Hank: How’s it going?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.150
John: Oh boy! We got a fish!

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.719
Hank: This is a very small ocean you’ve
put me in.

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:45.060
Hank: I don’t think so.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:54.930
John: So you’re our entertainment?

